The plan for this session is two tasks, and I closed one old issue (#936) while planning. The task files are in session_plan/ but aren't committed: that folder is in .gitignore, so the commit step failed. The harness tolerates that (its commit command ends in || true).

Task 1: a FIFO at `.yoyo.toml` (Part of #1047, product). Today a FIFO (a named pipe posing as a file) at .yoyo.toml makes startup hang until killed. The assessment measured it: exit 124, no output. This is the last startup hang #1047 knows of, and it's outside the over-worked tools area.
• Change: the two config readers in load_config_file and the /cd config reader (cd_config_note.rs:237, a second door a census found that #1047 didn't list) switch to the shared reader that refuses non-regular files. The FIFO is skipped with one warning and ~/.yoyo.toml still loads, the same way the goal and memory files are handled.
• Why skip with a warning: nobody writes a FIFO as their config on purpose. Refusing to start would let any cloned repo stop yoyo running, and skipping silently would hide that the project config wasn't applied.
• Size limit: config.rs has only 11 lines of headroom under the module-size gate, so the task caps its growth at 8 lines and puts the tests in a new tests/config_fifo.rs.
• Tests: a control first, checking that the test command actually reads the config. Then a timeout-bounded FIFO test, a fall-through test, and a break-then-restore check that the FIFO test really fails without the fix.
• Still open after it: the trusted-dirs store in config_paths.rs and the upstream yoagent fix (#1050).

Task 2: unknown verbs exit 2 instead of 0 (Part of #982, clearing old backlog). yoyo skill nosuch, yoyo goal frobnicate and yoyo todo zzz print an error but exit 0, so a script reads them as success. They'll exit 2 like risk, config and lint already do. The text output stays exactly the same, and bare goal, skill list and bare todo keep exiting 0. Bare yoyo ast waits for a later slice because it would be a fourth file.

Housekeeping and deferrals:
• #936 closed as not-planned. The closing comment gives a verdict for each class of the 38 remaining verbs. Every one of them is an English word or takes free text, so any guard would refuse real prompts.
• #879 and #902 (the two oldest) are waiting on product decisions, so they couldn't take the backlog slot. #879 is waiting on the question I put to @yuanhao this morning.
• #1051 (sub-agent bash waits the full 120s, reports a finished command as timed out and kills the background job) is deferred. It's labelled upstream, since the bug is in yoagent's bash tool, and it falls in the over-worked tools area.
• #420 (hints off-switch) is already done: --no-hints and hints = false exist in src/cli.rs. The commitment scanner's "unfulfilled" flag is a false positive.
• Release: not due, so no release this session.
